our team my man anyways the way Mason  explains it the players were paid a  salary based on the team standing in the  league but I read that contract and it  stipulates this salary as a bonus it's  not the salary in the way you and I  understand a salary it's literally a  bonus quote performance bonuses will be  awarded to the player based off their  placement in season three of overwatch  Caen  tenders Australia these bonuses will  take the form of a weekly salary for the  duration of contender season for and  weeks of practices leading up to the  season ten weeks in total the bonuses  are as follows  so basically first place you've got $150  second place you get $100 third fourth  you got 275 and then fifth through  eighth if in the standings you got fifty  bucks  okay now in the entire Mavericks history  the team hits second in one season  fourth in another season and then dead  last in this latest season and in  speaking to former Mavericks players  this salary was rarely paid on time week  to week in this contract it also states  that Mason apparently didn't have to pay  any payroll tax the players weren't  entitled to any sick leave and I quote  the player is not covered by National  Employment Standards this is basically a  list of Rights that everyone who works  in Australia gets and I don't think that  this dude gets to decide whether or not  those players have these rights and when  it comes to players leaving or  transferring to another team oh my god  doesn't get worse okay so if Mason or  the Mavericks were to axe a player  contract they'd have to give 45 days  written notice pretty standard stuff but  if a player wants to end a contract I  have no idea how much notice they had to  give because the contract switches  between seven and 14 days multiple times  and on top of that they have to give  Mason or the Mavericks $220 and if a  player wanted to transfer to a new team  that new team had to pay a transfer fee  of $6,000 okay but here's the thing if  